## MapLibre Style JSON Examples

### Example 1: Alpha Clipping Mask (Path B `"mask"` Blend Mode)
In this example, we have a city boundary shape and a complex striped pattern of line work. We want the striped pattern to render **only** inside the city boundary, without showing the white boundary polygon itself on the map.

Because we are using `"fill-blend-mode": "mask"`, the boundary layer acts as a clipping mask, regardless of layer order.

```json
{
  "version": 8,
  "sources": {
    "vector-map": {
      "type": "vector",
      "url": "mapbox://mapbox.mapbox-streets-v8"
    }
  },
  "layers": [
    {
      "id": "background",
      "type": "background",
      "paint": {
        "background-color": "#111111"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "city-mask-boundary",
      "type": "fill",
      "source": "vector-map",
      "source-layer": "boundary",
      "filter": ["==", "city", "Seattle"],
      "composite-group": "seattle-clipper",
      "paint": {
        "fill-color": "#ffffff",
        "fill-blend-mode": "mask"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "complex-road-patterns",
      "type": "line",
      "source": "vector-map",
      "source-layer": "road",
      "composite-group": "seattle-clipper",
      "paint": {
        "line-color": "#ff0077",
        "line-width": 3,
        "line-opacity": 0.8
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

---

### Example 2: Knockout / Clipping Holes (`"destination-out"`)
In this example, we want to cut clean "holes" through a dark overlay layer using building shapes, revealing the base map beneath.

```json
{
  "version": 8,
  "sources": {
    "vector-map": {
      "type": "vector",
      "url": "mapbox://mapbox.mapbox-streets-v8"
    }
  },
  "layers": [
    {
      "id": "satellite-base",
      "type": "raster",
      "source": "satellite-source"
    },
    {
      "id": "dark-shading-tint",
      "type": "fill",
      "source": "vector-map",
      "source-layer": "landuse",
      "composite-group": "knockout-group",
      "paint": {
        "fill-color": "#000000",
        "fill-opacity": 0.75
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "building-cutouts",
      "type": "fill",
      "source": "vector-map",
      "source-layer": "building",
      "composite-group": "knockout-group",
      "paint": {
        "fill-color": "#ffffff",
        "fill-blend-mode": "destination-out"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

---

### Example 3: Explicit Layer Root Property (`"composite-mask": true`)
If you want to keep the paint properties separate and purely declare the layer's mask semantic at the root of the layer, you can use the `"composite-mask": true` flag:

```json
{
  "id": "park-clipping-boundary",
  "type": "fill",
  "source": "vector-map",
  "source-layer": "landuse",
  "filter": ["==", "class", "park"],
  "composite-group": "park-details-group",
  "composite-mask": true,
  "paint": {
    "fill-color": "#ffffff"
  }
}
```

